From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DroidDeck <droiddeck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] event: with PROOT_EXIT_KILL and --kill-on-exit, tracees die
 with the tracer

--kill-on-exit takes the tracees down only when PRoot gets to run its own
cleanup, and SIGKILL never lets it: a PRoot killed by Android, the low
memory killer or its parent left every tracee running with no tracer, where
each syscall its seccomp filter traces fails with ENOSYS. With
PROOT_EXIT_KILL in PRoot's environment (and only then), the options PRoot
sets on its first tracee include PTRACE_O_EXITKILL, so the kernel kills
every tracee when PRoot exits, however it exits. That is the only
PTRACE_SETOPTIONS PRoot issues: each new tracee (fork, vfork, clone) is
attached by the kernel with its parent's options, this one included.
---
 src/compat.h       |  3 +++
 src/tracee/event.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/compat.h b/src/compat.h
index f69bc3f..2cad041 100644
--- a/src/compat.h
+++ b/src/compat.h
@@ -135,6 +135,9 @@
 #    ifndef PTRACE_O_TRACESECCOMP
 #        define PTRACE_O_TRACESECCOMP	0x00000080
 #    endif
+#    ifndef PTRACE_O_EXITKILL
+#        define PTRACE_O_EXITKILL	0x00100000
+#    endif
 #    ifndef PTRACE_EVENT_FORK
 #        define PTRACE_EVENT_FORK	1
 #    endif
diff --git a/src/tracee/event.c b/src/tracee/event.c
index c8f7801..0872955 100644
--- a/src/tracee/event.c
+++ b/src/tracee/event.c
@@ -467,6 +467,7 @@ int handle_tracee_event(Tracee *tracee,
 				PTRACE_O_TRACEEXEC	|
 				PTRACE_O_TRACECLONE	|
 				PTRACE_O_TRACEEXIT);
+			unsigned long exit_kill = 0;
 
 			/* Distinguish some events from others and
 			 * automatically trace each new process with
@@ -481,13 +482,24 @@ int handle_tracee_event(Tracee *tracee,
 
 			deliver_sigtrap = true;
 
+			/* PROOT_EXIT_KILL, with --kill-on-exit: the kernel
+			 * kills every tracee when PRoot exits, even when
+			 * PRoot itself is SIGKILLed and never gets to, so
+			 * none is left running untraced.  This is the only
+			 * place the options are set, on the first tracee:
+			 * the kernel attaches each new one (fork, vfork,
+			 * clone) with its parent's options, this one
+			 * included.  */
+			if (tracee->killall_on_exit && getenv("PROOT_EXIT_KILL") != NULL)
+				exit_kill = PTRACE_O_EXITKILL;
+
 			/* Try to enable seccomp mode 2...  */
 			status = ptrace(PTRACE_SETOPTIONS, tracee->pid, NULL,
-					default_ptrace_options | PTRACE_O_TRACESECCOMP);
+					default_ptrace_options | exit_kill | PTRACE_O_TRACESECCOMP);
 			if (status < 0) {
 				/* ... otherwise use default options only.  */
 				status = ptrace(PTRACE_SETOPTIONS, tracee->pid, NULL,
-						default_ptrace_options);
+						default_ptrace_options | exit_kill);
 				if (status < 0) {
 					note(tracee, ERROR, SYSTEM, "ptrace(PTRACE_SETOPTIONS)");
 					exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
